{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1660","published":"2026-03-20T11:10:41Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:40.494756939Z","upstream":["CVE-2025-66413"],"summary":"git security update","details":"Git is a free and open source distributed version control system designed to handle everything from small to very large projects with speed and efficiency. Git is easy to learn and has a tiny footprint with lightning fast performance. It outclasses SCM tools like Subversion, CVS, Perforce, and ClearCase with features like cheap local branching, convenient staging areas, and multiple workflows.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nGit for Windows is the Windows port of Git. Prior to 2.53.0(2), it is possible to obtain a user&apos;s NTLM hash by tricking them into cloning from a malicious server. Since NTLM hashing is weak, it is possible for the attacker to brute-force the user&apos;s account name and password. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.53.0(2).(CVE-2025-66413)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"git","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/git&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.43.0-11.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["git-2.43.0-11.oe2403.aarch64.rpm","git-core-2.43.0-11.oe2403.aarch64.rpm","git-daemon-2.43.0-11.oe2403.aarch64.rpm","git-debuginfo-2.43.0-11.oe2403.aarch64.rpm","git-debugsource-2.43.0-11.oe2403.aarch64.rpm","git-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","git-core-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","git-daemon-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","git-debuginfo-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","git-debugsource-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","git-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm","git-core-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm","git-daemon-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm","git-debuginfo-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm","git-debugsource-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm","git-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","git-core-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","git-daemon-2.43.0-11.oe2403sp3.aar